---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import GradeScale from '../components/GradeScale';

const title = "Grading Scale & GPA Converter | Pass My Finals";
const description = "Understand how your percentage maps to letter grades and GPA. Customizable scales for college and high school students.";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
	<main class="relative">
		<header class="pt-20 pb-12 text-center px-4 max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6">
			<h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-black tracking-tight text-black dark:text-white leading-tight">
				Grade <span class="text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-400 to-indigo-500">Scale</span>
			</h1>
			<p class="text-lg text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-400 font-medium">
				Master the conversion between percentages, letter grades, and grade points. Choose a preset or customize to match your school's policy.
			</p>
		</header>

		<section class="pb-20">
			<GradeScale client:load />
		</section>

		<section class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900/30 border-t border-gray-200 dark:border-white/5 py-16">
			<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 prose dark:prose-invert">
				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-black dark:text-white mb-6">Understanding Grading Scales</h2>
				<p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-slate-300">
					A grading scale is a system used to determine the letter grade a student receives based on their performance in a course. Different institutions use different scales, but the 4.0 scale is the most common in the United States.
				</p>
				<h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-black dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Why do scales vary?</h3>
				<p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-400">
					While many colleges follow the standard +/- system, some smaller schools or specific departments may use a flat scale (where an A- is not an option) or even a 7-point scale. Our tool allows you to adjust the minimum percentage required for each bracket to ensure accuracy.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>
